# The operator, 2026-10-11: "i have a ghost quarter up and it's my opponents
# turn, but the game won't let me respond with it?" Alice (seat 0) casts Raging
# Goblin off one of three Mountains; bob (seat 1) holds no cards and has an
# untapped Ghost Quarter beside a Forest. With the Goblin on the stack, Ghost
# Quarter's "{T}, Sacrifice: Destroy target land" is bob's to use, so his window
# is his to answer, not passed for him. `land-only-pass.state` is the control:
# the same cast with only a basic land on bob's side, where nothing but mana is
# there to use. `e2e/land-abilities.spec.ts`.
turn=1
activeplayer=human
activephase=MAIN1
humanlife=20
ailife=20
humanhand=Raging Goblin
humanbattlefield=Mountain;Mountain;Mountain
humanlibrary=Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain
humangraveyard=
aihand=
aibattlefield=Ghost Quarter;Forest
ailibrary=Forest;Forest;Forest;Forest;Forest;Forest
aigraveyard=
